From 0f983c5e930a1cda0e045d631e8b90d1ad50ee70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AliGram <aligram@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:47:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/67] feat(aligram): adjustable preservation limits (settings
 UI)

User-facing settings for the preservation limits, in the AliGram
section of the Experimental settings screen. Defaults reproduce
today's behavior exactly; nothing changes until the user touches a row.

- Video cap: one value for both networks (Default = 10 MB mobile /
  15 MB Wi-Fi; presets 10/15/25/50/75/100 MB) plus a free-form custom
  value, honored only at 1..100 MB (hard ceiling 100 MB); custom wins
  over the preset when valid.
- Document cap: one value for both networks (Default = 1 MB mobile /
  3 MB Wi-Fi; presets 1/3/5/10/25/50 MB).
- Max preserved files per chat: 10/25/50/100, default 25.
- Per-chat storage budget: 100/250/500/1000 MB, default 500 MB.
- Photos stay uncapped; roaming still blocks ingest; activation
  boundary, media set, and P/E/X matrix unchanged.

AliGramEligibility gains a pure Limits value type plus Limits-aware
sizeCapBytes/isWithinSizeCap/withinBudget overloads (legacy
signatures untouched); AliGramPreservation.limits() reads the NaConfig
entries and the two ingest sites use them. 5 new deterministic JVM
tests (80 total, 0 failures expected): defaults, video preset on both
networks, custom clamping (0/negative unset, 101+ capped at 100,
custom beats preset), document preset, adjustable budgets.
